    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Optimize the sliding window technique for finding the maximum sum of an SxS submatrix by improving memory locality and loop order.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Reordered loops to improve cache locality.\",\n    \"Removed unnecessary assertions.\",\n    \"Simplified the sliding window logic.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &matrix[i][j]);\\n\\n    int sum = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; i++)\\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; j++)\\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n    int mxSum = sum;\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; i++) {\\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; j++) {\\n            if (i == 0 && j == 0) continue;\\n            if (i == 0) {\\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\\n                    sum -= matrix[k][j - 1];\\n                    sum += matrix[k][j + s - 1];\\n                }\\n            } else if (j == 0) {\\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\\n                    sum -= matrix[i - 1][k];\\n                    sum += matrix[i + s - 1][k];\\n                }\\n            } else {\\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) {\\n                    sum -= matrix[i - 1][j + k - 1];\\n                    sum -= matrix[i + s - 1][j + k - 1];\\n                    sum += matrix[i + s - 1][j + k];\\n                    sum += matrix[i - 1][j + k];\\n                }\\n            }\\n            mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Reordered the loops to improve cache locality and simplified the sliding window logic to reduce redundant calculations.\"\n}"
